===Etymology===
Borrowed in the Middle Ages from a [[Low German]] variant of [[Theodoric]], Germanic ''þeud'' "people" + ''ric'' "ruler", and revived in the nineteenth century.<ref>Patrick Hanks and Flavia Hodges: A Concise Dictionary of First Names.Oxford University Press 2001.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
[[Rhymes:English:'dɛrɪk|'dɛrɪk]]
*: {{rhymes|ɛrɪk}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{given name|male|from=Germanic}}. Popular in the UK in mid-twentieth century.

